Virtualization means

One powerful Physical server will be divided into multiple VM's  (eg: VM1 and VM2 and VM3) 

example VM ware or Virtual box we can install multiple OS and it will work isolated and if one server having issue or crash it will
not impact for the another server or VM

example we have 3 services 

1. Payroll -first VM
2. HR    -- Second VM
3. Web Portal --3rd VM 

if virtualization not there we need to buy a separate physical servers for each 3 as a result  cost also increasing if ur using 20 to 30% usage 
and the storage , RAM and CPU also will be wasted in physical servers point of view (on-premises) 

1. Payroll -first physical server
2. HR    -- Second physical server
3. Web Portal --3rd physical server

example : 1 physical server is 5 Laksh and for 3 physical servers cost will be 15 lakshs 

but if we are using these 3 VM's on single physical server or machine cost will be reduced  and no need separate physical servers 

example in the cloud also we using virtualizations 

Hypervisor : it is placed B/W the Physical server and VM
and it is act as manager
It responsible for creating VM's and allocating Hardware resources to VM
It allocating how much CPU, RAM and STORAGE gives to VM

example: Xen and Microsoft Hyper-V

CPU --16 CORE

RAM --64 GB

STORAGE --1TB SSD 100GB

we have a 3 VM's Hypervisor will allocate 

1st VM---CPU+RAM+STORAGE     = 4CPU+16GB+200GB
2nd VM ---CPU+RAM+STORAGE      = 4CPU+16GB+300GB
3rd VM ---CPU+RAM+STORAGE      = 8CPU+32GB+500GB
